       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n**The problem:** The usual adult amlodipine dose is 2.5\u201310 mg by mouth once daily, and the maximum is 10 mg/day. 50 mg is five times the maximum. At that dose, amlodipine overdose can cause severe low blood pressure, shock, and noncardiogenic pulmonary edema. These effects can last a long time because the drug has a long half-life.\n\nThis looks like it could be a typo for **5 mg**, which is a common starting dose.\n\n**Can you confirm which you'd like?**\n1. **Amlodipine 5 mg by mouth once daily.** I can enter this right away.\n2. **A different dose within 2.5\u201310 mg.**\n3. **50 mg as written.** If this is really what you intend, please tell me the clinical reason so I can include it in the order note. Pharmacy review will very likely flag it."
