      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still haven't entered it. You've confirmed the dose, but I can't place an order for 5 times the maximum dose without a documented clinical reason. 50 mg/day of amlodipine isn't an accepted dose for any indication. At that level it causes the toxicity seen in overdose: refractory low blood pressure and shock, which can last a long time because of the drug's long half-life. Typos like 5 \u2192 50 are among the most common serious ordering errors, so I want to be sure this is intended.\n\n**You could:**\n- **Give me the clinical reason** (for example, a protocol or research study). I'll enter the order with that reason in the note so pharmacy can review it.\n- **Choose a standard dose instead**, such as amlodipine 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily. I can enter either one right away.\n- **Enter it yourself in the order system** if you want to proceed without a stated reason. That keeps it under your direct authorization and through the system's usual dose-limit override and pharmacy checks."
      }
